lifeos-nix patch f-projects-dormant — do not force-load USER/PROJECTS.md at startup

PROBLEM
  PROJECTS.md is upstream's per-project routing/resume file. Setup (activateImports)
  uncomments its `@`-import in CLAUDE.md, so it is force-loaded at every session start.
  Unlike the identity files it grows UNBOUNDED with project count: on a real multi-project
  install it measured ~53% of startup context (~19.5k tokens) while any given session touches
  exactly one project. Project/resume state is already available on-demand via ContextSearch
  (session registry + per-project ISAs) and per-project CLAUDE.md — the startup force-load
  duplicates a purpose better served lazily.

FIX (1 file) — change the DEFAULT to dormant, keep it opt-in
  InstallEngine.ts (activateImports; the logic ActivateImports.ts wraps) — skip
  `@LIFEOS/USER/PROJECTS.md`: leave it commented in CLAUDE.md instead of uncommenting it. A
  user who wants PROJECTS.md as a startup routing table can uncomment the line by hand; the
  capability is unchanged, only the default. All other identity imports activate as before.

  7.40.4 migration note (2026-08-27): the original patch had a SECOND hunk dropping
  "USER/PROJECTS.md" from settings.system.json postCompactRestore.fullFiles. 7.40.4 REMOVED
  the postCompactRestore mechanism from settings.system.json entirely (`grep -c
  postCompactRestore settings.system.json` == 0), so that hunk dissolved and is dropped —
  only the activateImports hunk remains, re-generated against 7.40.4's leaner activateImports.

VERIFICATION
  Post-install: CLAUDE.md still shows `# @LIFEOS/USER/PROJECTS.md` commented; the other
  identity imports are activated. Hunk via `git diff`, never hand-counted.

